  <!-- HTC Desire 510 (a11chl) on LineageOS 18.1: applied at a checkout made with
       repo init's reference option pointing at $HOME/Projects/Android/trees/tuna/lineage-18.1 (a new tree,
       e.g. $HOME/Projects/Android/trees/desire510-18.1), never layered onto the live tuna
       tree itself; see HTC-Desire510/notes/LINEAGE_18_1_PORT_PLAN.md
       section 1 for why (tuna.xml re-points frameworks/native, hardware/
       interfaces, and build/soong at tuna-only forks; a second local
       manifest cannot re-point the same paths a second way, and any tuna
       patch not gated by a BoardConfig flag would silently apply to an
       a11 lunch target too).

       The "oich" remote is the Oichkatzelesfrettschen fork holding this
       device's own commits. kernel/htc/a11 follows lineage-18.1-kernel,
       which carries the mpm-of modpost fix, the Android 11 binder, seccomp
       filter enforcement, sdcardfs, and the recovery-proven FunctionFS/AIO
       and mmap_rnd_bits series; that head boots TWRP 3.7 with adb.

       device/htc/msm8226-common's own lineage.dependencies (read via `gh
       api .../contents/lineage.dependencies?ref=lineage-18.1`) names two
       projects its BoardConfigCommon.mk/Android.bp include: qcom-common
       (the tree msm8226-common itself inherits from) and hardware/sony/
       timekeep. Neither carries an HTC-specific patch, so both are
       referenced straight from LineageOS at their lineage-18.1 tip, not
       forked; a fork is warranted only once this device needs to diverge
       from either.

       frameworks/base follows the fork's lineage-18.1, which adds the
       XTRA server list to gps_debug.conf: frameworks/base installs that
       file as a prebuilt_etc module, so a device copy of it collides in
       Kati.

       Every oich project tracks its merged lineage-18.1 base branch. The
       pinned heads build the image that runs SELinux enforcing with Wi-Fi,
       audio, the radio daemons and GNSS, zram, every USB function, the
       sensors, Bluetooth, the cameras, and the venus video core
       (notes/HARDWARE_REFERENCE_MATRIX.md, LineageOS 18.1 current state). -->
  <remote name="oich" fetch="https://github.com/Oichkatzelesfrettschen" review="github.com/Oichkatzelesfrettschen" />
  <remote name="lineage" fetch="https://github.com/LineageOS" />

  <remove-project name="LineageOS/android_build_soong" />
  <project path="build/soong" name="android_build_soong" remote="oich"
           revision="b44cd77eaec21eb0a1ddb3313584288db7382b1d"
           upstream="lineage-18.1" groups="pdk,tradefed">
    <linkfile src="root.bp" dest="Android.bp" />
